Z||000004||Uaana||08-28-2001||10:44 AM||||Well after a night to calm down.<BR>Talked with my mechanic this morning. worst case scenario around $500. Thank god I still have the rainbow marvel (spare transmission).<BR>And I've worked out a deal for a backup car so I can get to and from work.<BR>And I guess I won't get rid of it.. Too deep in now as it is.. <P>"I work, so I can fix the Fiero. So I can get to work. So I can make more money to fix the Fiero"  <P>Sound like anyone elses life?||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||08-28-2001||10:46 AM||||Patience... patience is what is always needed for your Fiero.  Just remember it's age.  My "GreenGT" has not always been a reliable driver.  Between the body, paint, engine, and tranny- my GT was in the shop for nearly 2 1/2 years straight!  In that period of time I was able to drive the car 1 week.  Patience.  Now, I've been driving it more than 2 straight summers with only minor irritations (exhaust, IAC, a few others...)<P>Patience is my only advice.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
