Z||000008||DreXteR||08-28-2001||04:59 PM||||Well, I dont know if this will help but here it is. I bougth my GT last year, really I havent ride it yet. Since I have it, has been in the garage getting fixed, very slow. I spend all my founds and what I dont have on it and barely doing progress. I lost the amount of money "invested". Somethimes I feel so angry that want to open the gate a crash the mo-fo fiero with my Grand Vitara, but then realize what is this all about. Its love, just that. I love my car eaven I didnt ride it yet. I spend lot of money and time fixing it but just do it rigth. I dont change one broke hose, I replace it all with the best quality I can afford. When finish the restauration I will know the car will be like take it out from the dealer whe it was new. That will be my satisfaction, besides kill all jap ricers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Take in cosideration the car has +15 years and it still runing. I know many "reliable cars" died after 8 or 9 yrs. As you can see its not that bad. Certanly the car is getting into what i call "existance limit". Where car life is done and you need to make it new. Dont expect to just fix some hoses and some cables expecting the car will continue 8 years more. Its time to make it reborn. By now I just did the front suspension with all it ralated new with performance parts. Now Im @ the rear end, expecting rebuild the engine. tranny, muffler, suspenssion and so on. And also bring it back with a new attitud - turbo intercooler. I see my car every day and feel sad about it, with the engine cradel and all stuff in the floor waiting there to be fixed and dont have suficient founds to do it. Then I just think in what it will become whe the job is done... .... .aaaaa.... I can imagine my self crusssing aside the beach with my wife inside this magnificent machine....<P>Dont loose the patience....keep it rigth.<P><BR>DreX<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/Fiero/Fiero1.jpg">  <BR>86 GT Turbo Intercooler Project - Total Restoration.||||reg||1
